From e6dedd374ab9cc4f8eb9af82f5fa62ace41a4829 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AAP Rebuild <aap-rebuild-bot@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:32:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] patch: add pod affinity support to EDA components
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Our own minimal affinity implementation (the AAP-81880 affinity feature ships
only in the downstream-private, UNLICENSED operator source, so we do not vendor
it — see the DEFERRED note in build.sh). This reproduces the capability from
licensed/standard sources only:

- CRD: add the standard Kubernetes corev1.Affinity schema (controller-gen
  output, Apache-2.0 k8s content — identical across all operators) to the 6
  components that support it (api, ui, event_stream, default_worker,
  activation_worker, worker; NOT scheduler, matching the bundle).
- defaults/main.yml: affinity: {} on the 5 deployed components.
- deployment templates: a guarded
    {% if combined_X.affinity is defined and combined_X.affinity|length>0 %}
  affinity passthrough (our own glue), mirroring the existing
  topology_spread_constraints block; combine_defaults wires combined_X.affinity
  automatically.

Does NOT include the downstream UI placement-reconcile task (#374), which
references combined_ui.affinity without a default and belongs to the private
feature set.
